{{- define "custom.custom.configuration.header" -}}
## Custom configuration
{{- end -}}

{{- define "custom.custom.configuration" -}}
{{ template "custom.custom.configuration.header" . }}

teslamate-abrp subscribes to TeslaMate's MQTT topics and forwards the car's
state to [A Better Route Planner](https://abetterrouteplanner.com). It has no
web UI or port. Point it at the same broker TeslaMate publishes to and give it
your ABRP user token:

```yaml
controllers:
  main:
    containers:
      main:
        env:
          MQTT_SERVER: mosquitto.home.svc
          CAR_NUMBER: "1"
          CAR_MODEL: tesla:my:19:bt37:awd

abrp:
  existingSecret: teslamate-abrp   # keys: USER_TOKEN, optionally MQTT_PASSWORD
```

The [teslamate](https://github.com/egeback/helm-charts/tree/main/charts/teslamate)
chart can also run the bridge as a sidecar; use this chart when TeslaMate is
deployed separately.
{{- end -}}
